        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fix system prompt types for Anthropic SDK",
        "summary": "Updated `system` parameter type in `claude.ts` and `main-prompt.ts` to accept `string | Array<TextBlockParam>`. Imported `TextBlockParam` from `@anthropic-ai/sdk/resources` to align with SDK expectations. Applied `as const` assertions to `type` and `cache_control` fields in `system-prompt.ts` to satisfy strict literal type checks. Scope limited to backend Claude integration files.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:32:01.953Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant's instructions can now be sent as either a single block of text or a structured list of text pieces with special labels, and the system now correctly expects those formats when talking to the AI engine. If you looked behind the scenes, you'd see this only affects the backend code that packages up prompts before sending them for processing, no visible change to how you use the product, but the internal messages are now formatted in a way the AI engine is ready to accept. This is live today as part of the latest backend deployment.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
