        "v": 5,
        "title": "Switch package manager from Yarn to Bun",
        "summary": "Repository scripts and documentation updated to use Bun instead of Yarn for dependency management and execution. Backend and npm-app package.json scripts now invoke `bun run` or `bun` directly, removing `ts-node` dependencies where possible. Knowledge base files reflect the new standard, instructing users to use `bun add`, `bun install`, and `bun run build`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:30:49.529Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You (the developer) now use Bun to run the project instead of Yarn. When you start the backend, build the app, or install dependencies, your commands use the faster Bun tool directly. The documentation and every start script inside the project have been rewritten to call Bun, so commands like `bun add`, `bun install`, and `bun run` replace all the old Yarn ones.",
